# Store state a `whip` run leaves in the working tree. The trailing `*` covers
# SQLite's `-wal` and `-shm` sidecars, which hold committed pages not yet
# checkpointed into the database file — every store opens in WAL mode, so they
# are always present next to a store that has been written.
#
# Scoped to the database files rather than the whole directory on purpose:
# `.whipplescript/skills/` is project content a user is meant to commit
# (spec/skills.md), and ignoring the directory would silently hide it.
**/.whipplescript/**/*.sqlite*
**/.whipplescript/*.sqlite*
# The file store `examples/file-store-demo.whip` declares. Running the examples
# writes into it, and `check-rule-coverage.sh` runs every fixture-runnable
# example — so wiring that script to a runner (2026-08-28) made this artifact
# routine. Scoped to the one demo root for the same reason as the carve-out
# above: an untracked file is invisible to the checks that read `git ls-files`,
# so it has to be ignored deliberately rather than left lying in the tree.
**/.whipplescript/filestore-demo/
.dev.vars
crates/whipplescript-host-do/worker/.wrangler/
# A Codex sidecar writes its startup transcript here when run from the repository
# root. It carries a ChatGPT account identifier, so it is ignored rather than left
# to be picked up by a `git add .` the way it was in #49.
error.log
